1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,520
I know you're tired.

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:07,420
Nothing here needs following — it's just
going to keep going.

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:16,120
A short book about Ruth to begin, then the
whole of First Samuel, slowly: Hannah,

4
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:18,920
Samuel, Saul, David.

5
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:21,800
Esther at the end, if you're still awake.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,500
Get comfortable and let your eyes close.

7
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:31,280
If you're waiting on something tonight, leave it
in the comments — people here pray through

8
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:32,220
them.

9
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:35,120
Subscribe if these readings help you
sleep.

10
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:41,160
Lord, I've been waiting on something long
enough that I've stopped saying it out loud.

11
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:42,940
It isn't a crisis.

12
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:47,380
It's the same thing, still unfinished, one
more evening.

13
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:52,340
I've asked before, and I don't have a
better way to ask tonight.

14
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:54,500
So I'm not going to try.

15
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,280
I'm too tired to make the case, and you
have already heard the case.

16
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:05,460
There is a woman at the beginning of this
book who prayed without making a sound — only

17
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:10,460
her lips moving, so that the priest
watching her thought something was wrong.

18
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:13,200
Nothing was answered that night.

19
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:17,460
She went back, and ate, and her face was
different anyway.

20
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:20,080
That is what I'm asking for.

21
00:01:20,700 --> 00:01:21,840
Not the answer yet.

22
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:26,760
The part where I set the thing down and it
stays down until morning.

23
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,020
Hold what I'm carrying.

24
00:01:29,980 --> 00:01:32,000
It isn't going anywhere you can't reach.

25
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:35,980
Let the reading be company rather than
instruction.

26
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:40,380
I'm not in a state to learn much tonight,
but I can be kept.

27
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:46,400
And for anyone else listening who has been
waiting longer than they expected — give them

28
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,700
a quiet night too.

29
00:01:48,660 --> 00:01:49,560
Amen.

30
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,720
Ruth, chapter one.

31
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:57,340
In the days when the judges judged, there
was a famine in the land.

32
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:04,280
A certain man of Bethlehem Judah went to live
in the country of Moab with his wife and

33
00:02:04,320 --> 00:02:05,220
his two sons.

34
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:10,320
The name of the man was Elimelech, and the
name of his wife Naomi.

35
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:16,500
The names of his two sons were Mahlon and
Chilion, Ephrathites of Bethlehem Judah.

36
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:20,260
They came into the country of Moab and
lived there.

37
00:02:20,300 --> 00:02:26,760
Elimelech, Naomi’s husband, died; and she
was left with her two sons.

38
00:02:27,186 --> 00:02:30,426
They took for themselves wives of the
women of Moab.

39
00:02:31,026 --> 00:02:35,886
The name of the one was Orpah, and the
name of the other was Ruth.

40
00:02:36,846 --> 00:02:38,886
They lived there about ten years.

41
00:02:38,926 --> 00:02:45,846
Mahlon and Chilion both died, and the
woman was bereaved of her two children and

42
00:02:45,886 --> 00:02:46,786
of her husband.

43
00:02:47,346 --> 00:02:52,766
Then she arose with her daughters-in-law, that
she might return from the country of Moab;

44
00:02:53,306 --> 00:02:58,666
for she had heard in the country of Moab
how the LORD had visited his people in giving

45
00:02:58,706 --> 00:02:59,606
them bread.

46
00:03:00,466 --> 00:03:05,146
She went out of the place where she was,
and her two daughters-in-law with her.

47
00:03:05,706 --> 00:03:08,426
They went on the way to return to the land
of Judah.

48
00:03:09,866 --> 00:03:16,346
Naomi said to her two daughters-in-law, “Go,
return each of you to her mother’s house.

49
00:03:17,206 --> 00:03:22,206
May the LORD deal kindly with you, as you
have dealt with the dead and with me.

50
00:03:22,706 --> 00:03:28,426
May The LORD grant you that you may find
rest, each of you in the house of her husband.”

51
00:03:29,486 --> 00:03:33,806
Then she kissed them, and they lifted up
their voices, and wept.

52
00:03:34,446 --> 00:03:39,506
They said to her, “No, but we will return
with you to your people.”

53
00:03:39,946 --> 00:03:42,706
Naomi said, “Go back, my daughters.

54
00:03:43,406 --> 00:03:45,126
Why do you want to go with me?

55
00:03:45,666 --> 00:03:49,486
Do I still have sons in my womb, that they
may be your husbands?

56
00:03:50,426 --> 00:03:56,126
Go back, my daughters, go your way; for I
am too old to have a husband.

57
00:03:56,626 --> 00:04:02,126
If I should say, ‘I have hope,’ if I
should even have a husband tonight, and should also

58
00:04:02,166 --> 00:04:05,726
bear sons, would you then wait until they
were grown?

59
00:04:06,226 --> 00:04:08,246
Would you then refrain from having
husbands?

60
00:04:09,186 --> 00:04:15,706
No, my daughters, for it grieves me
seriously for your sakes, for the LORD’s

61
00:04:15,746 --> 00:04:17,426
hand has gone out against me.”

62
00:04:18,506 --> 00:04:24,846
They lifted up their voices and wept
again; then Orpah kissed her mother-in-law, but

63
00:04:24,886 --> 00:04:26,206
Ruth stayed with her.

64
00:04:26,646 --> 00:04:32,206
She said, “Behold, your sister-in-law has
gone back to her people and to her god.

65
00:04:33,186 --> 00:04:35,166
Follow your sister-in-law.”

66
00:04:35,206 --> 00:04:41,686
Ruth said, “Don’t urge me to leave you,
and to return from following you, for where

67
00:04:41,726 --> 00:04:45,826
you go, I will go; and where you stay, I
will stay.

68
00:04:46,546 --> 00:04:50,666
Your people will be my people, and your
God my God.

69
00:04:51,011 --> 00:04:55,911
Where you die, I will die, and there I
will be buried.

70
00:04:57,031 --> 00:05:03,531
May The LORD do so to me, and more also,
if anything but death parts you and

71
00:05:03,571 --> 00:05:04,171
me.”

72
00:05:04,211 --> 00:05:09,391
When Naomi saw that she was determined to
go with her, she stopped urging her.

73
00:05:10,231 --> 00:05:12,991
So they both went until they came to
Bethlehem.

74
00:05:13,911 --> 00:05:19,351
When they had come to Bethlehem, all the
city was excited about them, and they asked,

75
00:05:20,171 --> 00:05:21,071
“Is this Naomi?”

76
00:05:21,951 --> 00:05:24,911
She said to them, “Don’t call me Naomi.

77
00:05:26,011 --> 00:05:30,191
Call me Mara, for the Almighty has dealt
very bitterly with me.

78
00:05:31,371 --> 00:05:35,371
I went out full, and the LORD has brought
me home again empty.

79
00:05:36,051 --> 00:05:42,251
Why do you call me Naomi, since the
LORD has testified against me, and the Almighty has

80
00:05:42,291 --> 00:05:43,191
afflicted me?”

81
00:05:43,791 --> 00:05:50,691
So Naomi returned, and Ruth the Moabitess,
her daughter-in-law, with her, who

82
00:05:50,731 --> 00:05:52,751
returned out of the country of Moab.

83
00:05:53,231 --> 00:05:56,151
They came to Bethlehem in the beginning of
barley harvest.

84
00:05:57,951 --> 00:05:59,411
Ruth, chapter two.

85
00:05:59,451 --> 00:06:06,711
Naomi had a relative of her husband’s, a
mighty man of wealth, of the family of Elimelech,

86
00:06:06,751 --> 00:06:08,451
and his name was Boaz.

87
00:06:09,431 --> 00:06:16,331
Ruth the Moabitess said to Naomi, “Let me
now go to the field, and glean amongst

88
00:06:16,371 --> 00:06:21,171
the ears of grain after him in whose sight
I find favour.”

89
00:06:21,211 --> 00:06:23,871
She said to her, “Go, my daughter.”

90
00:06:24,491 --> 00:06:30,411
She went, and came and gleaned in the
field after the reapers; and she happened to come

91
00:06:30,451 --> 00:06:36,811
to the portion of the field belonging to
Boaz, who was of the family of Elimelech.

92
00:06:36,851 --> 00:06:43,311
Behold, Boaz came from Bethlehem, and said
to the reapers, “May The LORD be with

93
00:06:43,351 --> 00:06:44,011
you.”

94
00:06:44,051 --> 00:06:46,891
They answered him, “May The LORD bless
you.”

95
00:06:47,811 --> 00:06:53,811
Then Boaz said to his servant who was
set over the reapers, “Whose young lady is this?”

96
00:06:54,411 --> 00:07:00,851
The servant who was set over the reapers
answered, “It is the Moabite lady who came back

97
00:07:00,891 --> 00:07:03,391
with Naomi out of the country of Moab.

98
00:07:03,871 --> 00:07:09,311
She said, ‘Please let me glean and gather
after the reapers amongst the sheaves.’

99
00:07:10,071 --> 00:07:16,171
So she came, and has continued even from
the morning until now, except that she rested

100
00:07:16,211 --> 00:07:17,471
a little in the house.”

101
00:07:18,711 --> 00:07:21,951
Then Boaz said to Ruth, “Listen, my
daughter.

102
00:07:22,302 --> 00:07:28,682
Don’t go to glean in another field, and don’t
go from here, but stay here close to my

103
00:07:28,722 --> 00:07:29,622
maidens.

104
00:07:30,162 --> 00:07:34,582
Let your eyes be on the field that they
reap, and go after them.

105
00:07:35,422 --> 00:07:38,542
Haven’t I commanded the young men not to
touch you?

106
00:07:38,582 --> 00:07:44,662
When you are thirsty, go to the vessels,
and drink from that which the young men have

107
00:07:44,702 --> 00:07:45,962
drawn.”

108
00:07:46,002 --> 00:07:52,682
Then she fell on her face and bowed
herself to the ground, and said to him, “Why

109
00:07:52,722 --> 00:07:58,442
have I found favour in your sight, that you
should take knowledge of me, since I am a

110
00:07:58,482 --> 00:07:59,382
foreigner?”

111
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:05,422
Boaz answered her, “I have been told all
about what you have done for your mother-in-law

112
00:08:05,462 --> 00:08:11,162
since the death of your husband, and how
you have left your father, your mother, and

113
00:08:11,202 --> 00:08:15,602
the land of your birth, and have come to a
people that you didn’t know before.

114
00:08:16,402 --> 00:08:22,622
May the LORD repay your work, and a full
reward be given to you from the LORD, the God

115
00:08:22,662 --> 00:08:26,462
of Israel, under whose wings you have come
to take refuge.”

116
00:08:27,402 --> 00:08:33,622
Then she said, “Let me find favour in your
sight, my lord, because you have comforted

117
00:08:33,662 --> 00:08:39,562
me, and because you have spoken kindly to your
servant, though I am not as one of your

118
00:08:39,602 --> 00:08:40,502
servants.”

119
00:08:41,082 --> 00:08:47,622
At meal time Boaz said to her, “Come here,
and eat some bread, and dip your morsel

120
00:08:47,662 --> 00:08:48,562
in the vinegar.”

121
00:08:48,862 --> 00:08:52,882
She sat beside the reapers, and they
passed her parched grain.

122
00:08:54,002 --> 00:08:57,622
She ate, was satisfied, and left some of
it.

123
00:08:58,542 --> 00:09:05,082
When she had risen up to glean, Boaz
commanded his young men, saying, “Let her glean

124
00:09:05,122 --> 00:09:08,442
even amongst the sheaves, and don’t
reproach her.

125
00:09:08,882 --> 00:09:12,642
Also pull out some for her from the
bundles, and leave it.

126
00:09:13,482 --> 00:09:15,942
Let her glean, and don’t rebuke her.”

127
00:09:17,122 --> 00:09:22,782
So she gleaned in the field until evening;
and she beat out that which she had gleaned,

128
00:09:23,122 --> 00:09:25,062
and it was about an ephah of barley.

129
00:09:26,002 --> 00:09:28,522
She took it up, and went into the city.

130
00:09:29,182 --> 00:09:34,222
Then her mother-in-law saw what she had gleaned;
and she brought out and gave to her

131
00:09:34,782 --> 00:09:37,342
that which she had left after she had
enough.

132
00:09:38,342 --> 00:09:42,362
Her mother-in-law said to her, “Where have
you gleaned today?

133
00:09:43,462 --> 00:09:44,362
Where have you worked?

134
00:09:44,626 --> 00:09:47,766
Blessed be he who noticed you.”

135
00:09:47,806 --> 00:09:53,586
She told her mother-in-law with whom she had
worked, “The man’s name with whom I worked

136
00:09:53,626 --> 00:09:55,226
today is Boaz.”

137
00:09:56,386 --> 00:10:02,786
Naomi said to her daughter-in-law, “May he be
blessed by the LORD, who has not abandoned

138
00:10:02,826 --> 00:10:05,506
his kindness to the living and to the
dead.”

139
00:10:06,186 --> 00:10:12,546
Naomi said to her, “The man is a close
relative to us, one of our near kinsmen.”

140
00:10:13,226 --> 00:10:19,706
Ruth the Moabitess said, “Yes, he said to
me, ‘You shall stay close to my

141
00:10:19,746 --> 00:10:26,066
young men until they have finished all
my harvest.’” Naomi said to Ruth her daughter-in-law,

142
00:10:26,106 --> 00:10:31,526
“It is good, my daughter, that you go out
with his maidens, and that they not meet you

143
00:10:31,566 --> 00:10:32,686
in any other field.”

144
00:10:33,606 --> 00:10:39,686
So she stayed close to the maidens of Boaz,
to glean to the end of barley harvest and

145
00:10:39,726 --> 00:10:43,426
of wheat harvest; and she lived with her
mother-in-law.

146
00:10:43,466 --> 00:10:46,246
Ruth, chapter three.

147
00:10:46,286 --> 00:10:52,846
Naomi her mother-in-law said to her, “My
daughter, shall I not seek rest for you,

148
00:10:53,506 --> 00:10:54,946
that it may be well with you?

149
00:10:55,846 --> 00:11:00,206
Now isn’t Boaz our kinsman, with whose
maidens you were?

150
00:11:00,626 --> 00:11:05,246
Behold, he will be winnowing barley
tonight on the threshing floor.

151
00:11:05,966 --> 00:11:12,486
Therefore wash yourself, anoint yourself,
get dressed, and go down to the threshing

152
00:11:12,526 --> 00:11:19,166
floor; but don’t make yourself known to the
man until he has finished eating and drinking.

153
00:11:20,326 --> 00:11:25,506
It shall be, when he lies down, that you
shall note the place where he is lying.

154
00:11:26,306 --> 00:11:30,266
Then you shall go in, uncover his feet,
and lie down.

155
00:11:31,186 --> 00:11:33,126
Then he will tell you what to do.”

156
00:11:33,706 --> 00:11:37,566
She said to her, “All that you say, I will
do.”

157
00:11:38,686 --> 00:11:43,786
She went down to the threshing floor, and
did everything that her mother-in-law told

158
00:11:43,826 --> 00:11:44,586
her.

159
00:11:44,626 --> 00:11:51,126
When Boaz had eaten and drunk, and his heart
was merry, he went to lie down at the end

160
00:11:51,166 --> 00:11:52,226
of the heap of grain.

161
00:11:53,186 --> 00:11:57,306
She came softly, uncovered his feet, and
lay down.

162
00:11:58,086 --> 00:12:04,686
At midnight, the man was startled and
turned himself; and behold, a woman lay

163
00:12:04,726 --> 00:12:05,626
at his feet.

164
00:12:06,246 --> 00:12:08,206
He said, “Who are you?”

165
00:12:08,786 --> 00:12:11,666
She answered, “I am Ruth your servant.

166
00:12:12,191 --> 00:12:18,191
Therefore spread the corner of your garment over
your servant; for you are a near kinsman.”

167
00:12:18,991 --> 00:12:22,451
He said, “You are blessed by the LORD, my
daughter.

168
00:12:23,171 --> 00:12:29,071
You have shown more kindness in the latter
end than at the beginning, because you didn’t

169
00:12:29,111 --> 00:12:32,071
follow young men, whether poor or rich.

170
00:12:32,891 --> 00:12:35,111
Now, my daughter, don’t be afraid.

171
00:12:35,991 --> 00:12:42,171
I will do to you all that you say; for all
the city of my people knows that you are a

172
00:12:42,211 --> 00:12:43,111
worthy woman.

173
00:12:43,951 --> 00:12:46,931
Now it is true that I am a near kinsman.

174
00:12:47,551 --> 00:12:50,891
However, there is a kinsman nearer than I.

175
00:12:51,471 --> 00:12:57,371
Stay this night, and in the morning, if he
will perform for you the part of a kinsman,

176
00:12:57,631 --> 00:12:58,531
good.

177
00:12:58,811 --> 00:13:00,551
Let him do the kinsman’s duty.

178
00:13:01,591 --> 00:13:07,311
But if he will not do the duty of a kinsman
for you, then I will do the duty of a kinsman

179
00:13:07,351 --> 00:13:09,551
for you, as the LORD lives.

180
00:13:09,911 --> 00:13:11,531
Lie down until the morning.”

181
00:13:12,191 --> 00:13:17,931
She lay at his feet until the morning,
then she rose up before one could discern another.

182
00:13:18,851 --> 00:13:23,651
For he said, “Let it not be known that the
woman came to the threshing floor.”

183
00:13:24,551 --> 00:13:28,491
He said, “Bring the mantle that is on you,
and hold it.”

184
00:13:29,151 --> 00:13:35,691
She held it; and he measured six measures of
barley, and laid it on her; then he went

185
00:13:35,731 --> 00:13:36,631
into the city.

186
00:13:37,571 --> 00:13:42,091
When she came to her mother-in-law, she
said, “How did it go, my daughter?”

187
00:13:43,011 --> 00:13:45,551
She told her all that the man had done for
her.

188
00:13:46,211 --> 00:13:52,771
She said, “He gave me these six measures of
barley; for he said, ‘Don’t go empty to your

189
00:13:52,811 --> 00:13:59,271
mother-in-law.’” Then she said, “Wait, my
daughter, until you know what will happen;

190
00:14:00,171 --> 00:14:03,671
for the man will not rest until he has
settled this today.”

191
00:14:04,611 --> 00:14:07,231
Ruth, chapter four.

192
00:14:07,271 --> 00:14:10,371
Now Boaz went up to the gate and sat down
there.

193
00:14:10,971 --> 00:14:15,091
Behold, the near kinsman of whom Boaz
spoke came by.

194
00:14:16,171 --> 00:14:20,511
Boaz said to him, “Come over here, friend,
and sit down!”

195
00:14:21,311 --> 00:14:23,431
He came over, and sat down.

196
00:14:24,191 --> 00:14:30,591
Boaz took ten men of the elders of the
city, and said, “Sit down here,” and they sat

197
00:14:30,631 --> 00:14:31,531
down.

198
00:14:31,851 --> 00:14:38,651
He said to the near kinsman, “Naomi, who has
come back out of the country of Moab, is

199
00:14:38,691 --> 00:14:41,751
selling the parcel of land, which was our
brother Elimelech’s.

200
00:14:42,925 --> 00:14:49,145
I thought I should tell you, saying, ‘Buy
it before those who sit here, and before the

201
00:14:49,185 --> 00:14:50,445
elders of my people.’

202
00:14:51,365 --> 00:14:57,945
If you will redeem it, redeem it; but if
you will not redeem it, then tell me, that

203
00:14:57,985 --> 00:14:58,885
I may know.

204
00:14:59,645 --> 00:15:04,185
For there is no one to redeem it besides
you; and I am after you.”

205
00:15:04,545 --> 00:15:06,885
He said, “I will redeem it.”

206
00:15:07,465 --> 00:15:14,045
Then Boaz said, “On the day you buy the
field from the hand of Naomi, you must

207
00:15:14,085 --> 00:15:20,585
buy it also from Ruth the Moabitess, the wife
of the dead, to raise up the name of the

208
00:15:20,625 --> 00:15:21,585
dead on his inheritance.”

209
00:15:22,645 --> 00:15:28,865
The near kinsman said, “I can’t redeem it
for myself, lest I endanger my own inheritance.

210
00:15:30,065 --> 00:15:34,365
Take my right of redemption for yourself;
for I can’t redeem it.”

211
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:39,745
Now this was the custom in former time in
Israel concerning redeeming and concerning

212
00:15:39,785 --> 00:15:46,285
exchanging, to confirm all things: a man
took off his sandal, and gave it to

213
00:15:46,325 --> 00:15:51,105
his neighbour; and this was the way of
formalizing transactions in Israel.

214
00:15:51,685 --> 00:15:58,105
So the near kinsman said to Boaz, “Buy
it for yourself,” then he took off his sandal.

215
00:15:58,845 --> 00:16:05,365
Boaz said to the elders and to all the
people, “You are witnesses today, that I

216
00:16:05,405 --> 00:16:10,845
have bought all that was Elimelech’s, and
all that was Chilion’s and Mahlon’s, from the

217
00:16:10,885 --> 00:16:11,785
hand of Naomi.

218
00:16:12,385 --> 00:16:18,865
Moreover, Ruth the Moabitess, the wife of
Mahlon, I have purchased to be my

219
00:16:18,905 --> 00:16:24,785
wife, to raise up the name of the dead on
his inheritance, that the name of the dead

220
00:16:24,825 --> 00:16:29,485
may not be cut off from amongst his
brothers and from the gate of his place.

221
00:16:30,425 --> 00:16:32,085
You are witnesses today.”

222
00:16:32,645 --> 00:16:37,485
All the people who were in the gate, and
the elders, said, “We are witnesses.

223
00:16:38,665 --> 00:16:44,365
May the LORD make the woman who has come
into your house like Rachel and like Leah, which

224
00:16:44,405 --> 00:16:50,285
both built the house of Israel; and treat
you worthily in Ephrathah, and be famous in

225
00:16:50,325 --> 00:16:51,225
Bethlehem.

226
00:16:51,705 --> 00:16:57,485
Let your house be like the house of Perez,
whom Tamar bore to Judah, of the offspring

227
00:16:57,525 --> 00:17:00,305
which the LORD will give you by this young
woman.”

228
00:17:00,728 --> 00:17:07,528
So Boaz took Ruth and she became his wife;
and he went in to her, and the LORD enabled

229
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:10,368
her to conceive, and she bore a son.

230
00:17:11,568 --> 00:17:17,608
The women said to Naomi, “Blessed be the LORD,
who has not left you today without a near

231
00:17:17,648 --> 00:17:18,548
kinsman.

232
00:17:18,908 --> 00:17:21,248
Let his name be famous in Israel.

233
00:17:22,128 --> 00:17:29,088
He shall be to you a restorer of life
and sustain you in your old age; for your daughter-in-law,

234
00:17:29,128 --> 00:17:34,288
who loves you, who is better to you than
seven sons, has given birth to him.”

235
00:17:34,708 --> 00:17:39,788
Naomi took the child, laid him in her
bosom, and became nurse to him.

236
00:17:40,388 --> 00:17:45,788
The women, her neighbours, gave him a
name, saying, “A son is born to Naomi”.

237
00:17:46,808 --> 00:17:48,108
They named him Obed.

238
00:17:48,628 --> 00:17:51,888
He is the father of Jesse, the father of
David.

239
00:17:51,928 --> 00:17:58,868
Now this is the history of the generations
of Perez: Perez became the father of Hezron,

240
00:17:58,908 --> 00:18:05,808
and Hezron became the father of Ram, and
Ram became the father of Amminadab, and Amminadab

241
00:18:05,848 --> 00:18:12,428
became the father of Nahshon, and Nahshon
became the father of Salmon, and Salmon became

242
00:18:12,468 --> 00:18:19,228
the father of Boaz, and Boaz became the
father of Obed, and Obed became the father

243
00:18:19,268 --> 00:18:22,608
of Jesse, and Jesse became the father of
David.

244
00:18:22,648 --> 00:18:26,568
First Samuel, chapter one.

245
00:18:26,608 --> 00:18:32,928
Now there was a certain man of Ramathaim
Zophim, of the hill country of Ephraim, and

246
00:18:32,968 --> 00:18:39,508
his name was Elkanah, the son of Jeroham,
the son of Elihu, the son of Tohu,

247
00:18:39,948 --> 00:18:42,248
the son of Zuph, an Ephraimite.

248
00:18:42,288 --> 00:18:44,088
He had two wives.

249
00:18:44,828 --> 00:18:49,108
The name of one was Hannah, and the name
of the other Peninnah.

250
00:18:49,148 --> 00:18:52,588
Peninnah had children, but Hannah had no
children.

251
00:18:53,488 --> 00:18:59,468
This man went up out of his city from year
to year to worship and to sacrifice to the

252
00:18:59,508 --> 00:19:01,068
LORD of Armies in Shiloh.

253
00:19:01,648 --> 00:19:07,168
The two sons of Eli, Hophni and Phinehas,
priests to the LORD, were there.

254
00:19:08,028 --> 00:19:14,488
When the day came that Elkanah sacrificed,
he gave portions to Peninnah his wife and

255
00:19:14,528 --> 00:19:20,188
to all her sons and her daughters; but he
gave a double portion to Hannah, for he loved

256
00:19:20,228 --> 00:19:23,008
Hannah, but the LORD had shut up her womb.

257
00:19:23,688 --> 00:19:29,868
Her rival provoked her severely, to irritate her,
because the LORD had shut up her womb.

258
00:19:30,281 --> 00:19:36,101
So year by year, when she went up to the
LORD’s house, her rival provoked her.

259
00:19:37,141 --> 00:19:39,661
Therefore she wept, and didn’t eat.

260
00:19:39,701 --> 00:19:45,401
Elkanah her husband said to her, “Hannah,
why do you weep?

261
00:19:46,021 --> 00:19:46,921
Why don’t you eat?

262
00:19:47,701 --> 00:19:48,921
Why is your heart grieved?

263
00:19:49,941 --> 00:19:52,081
Am I not better to you than ten sons?”

264
00:19:52,901 --> 00:19:57,121
So Hannah rose up after they had finished
eating and drinking in Shiloh.

265
00:19:57,941 --> 00:20:02,961
Now Eli the priest was sitting on his seat
by the doorpost of the LORD’s temple.

266
00:20:03,961 --> 00:20:08,581
She was in bitterness of soul, and prayed
to the LORD, weeping bitterly.

267
00:20:09,521 --> 00:20:15,561
She vowed a vow, and said, “LORD of
Armies, if you will indeed look at the affliction

268
00:20:15,601 --> 00:20:21,781
of your servant and remember me, and not
forget your servant, but will give to your servant

269
00:20:21,821 --> 00:20:28,181
a boy, then I will give him to the LORD
all the days of his life, and no razor shall

270
00:20:28,221 --> 00:20:29,161
come on his head.”

271
00:20:29,661 --> 00:20:33,661
As she continued praying before the LORD,
Eli saw her mouth.

272
00:20:34,641 --> 00:20:36,521
Now Hannah spoke in her heart.

273
00:20:37,521 --> 00:20:40,921
Only her lips moved, but her voice was not
heard.

274
00:20:41,901 --> 00:20:43,961
Therefore Eli thought she was drunk.

275
00:20:45,021 --> 00:20:48,241
Eli said to her, “How long will you be
drunk?

276
00:20:49,121 --> 00:20:50,021
Get rid of your wine!”

277
00:20:50,561 --> 00:20:55,581
Hannah answered, “No, my lord, I am a
woman of a sorrowful spirit.

278
00:20:56,421 --> 00:21:02,081
I have not been drinking wine or strong drink,
but I poured out my soul before the LORD.

279
00:21:02,941 --> 00:21:08,161
Don’t consider your servant a wicked woman; for
I have been speaking out of the abundance

280
00:21:08,201 --> 00:21:10,501
of my complaint and my provocation.”

281
00:21:11,581 --> 00:21:18,081
Then Eli answered, “Go in peace; and may
the God of Israel grant your petition that you

282
00:21:18,121 --> 00:21:19,021
have asked of him.”

283
00:21:20,001 --> 00:21:23,801
She said, “Let your servant find favour in
your sight.”

284
00:21:24,841 --> 00:21:31,221
So the woman went her way and ate; and her
facial expression wasn’t sad any more.

285
00:21:31,261 --> 00:21:37,021
They rose up in the morning early and
worshipped the LORD, then returned and came to

286
00:21:37,061 --> 00:21:39,181
their house to Ramah.

287
00:21:39,221 --> 00:21:43,401
Then Elkanah knew Hannah his wife; and the
LORD remembered her.

288
00:21:44,421 --> 00:21:51,441
When the time had come, Hannah conceived, and
bore a son; and she named him Samuel, saying,

289
00:21:52,481 --> 00:21:54,381
“Because I have asked him of the LORD.”

290
00:21:54,708 --> 00:22:00,908
The man Elkanah, and all his house, went
up to offer to the LORD the yearly sacrifice

291
00:22:00,948 --> 00:22:02,108
and his vow.

292
00:22:03,368 --> 00:22:09,528
But Hannah didn’t go up, for she said
to her husband, “Not until the child is weaned;

293
00:22:10,448 --> 00:22:15,108
then I will bring him, that he may appear
before the LORD, and stay there forever.”

294
00:22:15,148 --> 00:22:20,148
Elkanah her husband said to her, “Do what
seems good to you.

295
00:22:20,588 --> 00:22:25,408
Wait until you have weaned him; only may
the LORD establish his word.”

296
00:22:26,468 --> 00:22:30,428
So the woman waited and nursed her son
until she weaned him.

297
00:22:30,848 --> 00:22:36,548
When she had weaned him, she took him up
with her, with three bulls, and one ephah of

298
00:22:36,588 --> 00:22:42,308
meal, and a container of wine, and brought
him to the LORD’s house in Shiloh.

299
00:22:42,968 --> 00:22:44,408
The child was young.

300
00:22:45,188 --> 00:22:48,168
They killed the bull, and brought the
child to Eli.

301
00:22:48,948 --> 00:22:55,568
She said, “Oh, my lord, as your soul
lives, my lord, I am the woman who stood

302
00:22:55,608 --> 00:22:58,088
by you here, praying to the LORD.

303
00:22:58,688 --> 00:23:04,248
I prayed for this child, and the LORD has
given me my petition which I asked of him.

304
00:23:05,108 --> 00:23:07,688
Therefore I have also given him to the
LORD.

305
00:23:08,308 --> 00:23:11,208
As long as he lives he is given to the
LORD.”

306
00:23:11,828 --> 00:23:13,248
He worshipped the LORD there.

307
00:23:14,248 --> 00:23:16,758
First Samuel, chapter two.

308
00:23:16,798 --> 00:23:21,468
Hannah prayed, and said, “My heart exults
in the LORD!

309
00:23:22,188 --> 00:23:24,068
My horn is exalted in the LORD.

310
00:23:24,828 --> 00:23:29,468
My mouth is enlarged over my enemies,
because I rejoice in your salvation.

311
00:23:30,508 --> 00:23:36,788
There is no one as holy as the LORD, for
there is no one besides you, nor is there any

312
00:23:36,828 --> 00:23:38,108
rock like our God.

313
00:23:39,208 --> 00:23:41,868
“Don’t keep talking so exceedingly
proudly.

314
00:23:42,748 --> 00:23:47,108
Don’t let arrogance come out of your
mouth, for the LORD is a God of knowledge.

315
00:23:48,008 --> 00:23:49,648
By him actions are weighed.

316
00:23:50,508 --> 00:23:52,368
“The bows of the mighty men are broken.

317
00:23:53,248 --> 00:23:55,448
Those who stumbled are armed with
strength.

318
00:23:56,368 --> 00:23:59,428
Those who were full have hired themselves
out for bread.

319
00:24:00,328 --> 00:24:02,188
Those who were hungry are satisfied.

320
00:24:03,208 --> 00:24:05,728
Yes, the barren has borne seven.

321
00:24:06,408 --> 00:24:08,808
She who has many children languishes.

322
00:24:09,668 --> 00:24:11,508
“The LORD kills and makes alive.

323
00:24:12,288 --> 00:24:14,868
He brings down to Sheol and brings up.

324
00:24:15,828 --> 00:24:18,168
The LORD makes poor and makes rich.

325
00:24:19,008 --> 00:24:21,748
He brings low, he also lifts up.

326
00:24:22,608 --> 00:24:25,088
He raises up the poor out of the dust.

327
00:24:25,544 --> 00:24:31,804
He lifts up the needy from the dunghill to
make them sit with princes and inherit the

328
00:24:31,844 --> 00:24:32,744
throne of glory.

329
00:24:34,084 --> 00:24:36,324
For the pillars of the earth are the
LORD’s.

330
00:24:37,204 --> 00:24:39,004
He has set the world on them.

331
00:24:40,044 --> 00:24:45,444
He will keep the feet of his holy ones,
but the wicked will be put to silence in darkness;

332
00:24:46,344 --> 00:24:48,484
for no man will prevail by strength.

333
00:24:49,484 --> 00:24:52,844
Those who strive with the LORD shall be
broken to pieces.

334
00:24:53,644 --> 00:24:55,744
He will thunder against them in the sky.

335
00:24:56,804 --> 00:24:59,224
“The LORD will judge the ends of the
earth.

336
00:25:00,004 --> 00:25:04,404
He will give strength to his king, and
exalt the horn of his anointed.”

337
00:25:04,444 --> 00:25:07,044
Elkanah went to Ramah to his house.

338
00:25:07,684 --> 00:25:10,624
The child served the LORD before Eli the
priest.

339
00:25:11,644 --> 00:25:14,324
Now the sons of Eli were wicked men.

340
00:25:15,284 --> 00:25:16,424
They didn’t know the LORD.

341
00:25:17,464 --> 00:25:25,084
The custom of

342
00:25:25,124 --> 00:25:25,424
the priests with the people was that
when anyone offered a sacrifice, the priest’s servant

343
00:25:25,464 --> 00:25:30,544
came while the meat was boiling, with a fork
of three teeth in his hand; and he stabbed

344
00:25:30,584 --> 00:25:34,744
it into the pan, or kettle, or cauldron,
or pot.

345
00:25:35,964 --> 00:25:38,964
The priest took all that the fork brought
up for himself.

346
00:25:40,164 --> 00:25:43,964
They did this to all the Israelites who
came there to Shiloh.

347
00:25:44,384 --> 00:25:50,924
Yes, before they burnt the fat, the priest’s
servant came, and said to the man who

348
00:25:50,964 --> 00:25:57,604
sacrificed, “Give meat to roast for the
priest; for he will not accept boiled meat

349
00:25:57,644 --> 00:25:59,024
from you, but raw.”

350
00:25:59,564 --> 00:26:05,564
If the man said to him, “Let the fat be
burnt first, and then take as much as your soul

351
00:26:05,604 --> 00:26:12,144
desires;” then he would say, “No, but you
shall give it to me now; and

352
00:26:12,184 --> 00:26:14,564
if not, I will take it by force.”

353
00:26:15,604 --> 00:26:21,764
The sin of the young men was very great
before the LORD; for the men despised the LORD’s

354
00:26:21,804 --> 00:26:22,704
offering.

355
00:26:23,004 --> 00:26:29,704
But Samuel ministered before the LORD,
being a child, clothed with a linen ephod.

356
00:26:29,744 --> 00:26:35,464
Moreover his mother made him a little robe, and
brought it to him from year to year when

357
00:26:35,504 --> 00:26:39,104
she came up with her husband to offer the
yearly sacrifice.

358
00:26:40,384 --> 00:26:46,864
Eli blessed Elkanah and his wife, and said,
“May The LORD give you offspring from this

359
00:26:46,904 --> 00:26:50,004
woman for the petition which was asked of
the LORD.”

360
00:26:50,333 --> 00:26:52,153
Then they went to their own home.

361
00:26:53,393 --> 00:26:59,173
The LORD visited Hannah, and she conceived
and bore three sons and two daughters.

362
00:27:00,133 --> 00:27:02,673
The child Samuel grew before the LORD.

363
00:27:03,933 --> 00:27:10,693
Now Eli was very old; and he heard all
that his sons did to all Israel, and

364
00:27:10,733 --> 00:27:14,853
how that they slept with the women who
served at the door of the Tent of Meeting.

365
00:27:15,793 --> 00:27:19,333
He said to them, “Why do you do such
things?

366
00:27:20,273 --> 00:27:23,233
For I hear of your evil dealings from all
these people.

367
00:27:24,013 --> 00:27:28,193
No, my sons; for it is not a good report
that I hear!

368
00:27:28,653 --> 00:27:30,753
You make the LORD’s people disobey.

369
00:27:31,673 --> 00:27:38,333
If one man sins against another, God will judge
him; but if a man sins against the LORD,

370
00:27:39,093 --> 00:27:40,553
who will intercede for him?”

371
00:27:42,473 --> 00:27:47,473
Notwithstanding, they didn’t listen to the voice
of their father, because the LORD intended

372
00:27:47,513 --> 00:27:48,413
to kill them.

373
00:27:49,093 --> 00:27:55,713
The child Samuel grew on, and increased in
favour both with the LORD and also with men.

374
00:27:56,993 --> 00:28:03,873
A man of God came to Eli and said to him,
“The LORD says, ‘Did I reveal myself to

375
00:28:03,913 --> 00:28:08,413
the house of your father when they were in
Egypt in bondage to Pharaoh’s house?

376
00:28:08,453 --> 00:28:14,673
Didn’t I choose him out of all the tribes of
Israel to be my priest, to go up to my altar,

377
00:28:15,313 --> 00:28:18,713
to burn incense, to wear an ephod before
me?

378
00:28:19,413 --> 00:28:24,153
Didn’t I give to the house of your
father all the offerings of the children of Israel

379
00:28:24,193 --> 00:28:25,313
made by fire?

380
00:28:25,853 --> 00:28:32,573
Why do you kick at my sacrifice and at
my offering, which I have commanded in my habitation,

381
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:39,413
and honour your sons above me, to make
yourselves fat with the best of all the offerings

382
00:28:39,453 --> 00:28:41,053
of Israel my people?’

383
00:28:41,613 --> 00:28:48,273
“Therefore the LORD, the God of Israel,
says, ‘I said indeed that your house and

384
00:28:48,313 --> 00:28:51,413
the house of your father should walk
before me forever.’

385
00:28:52,333 --> 00:28:59,053
But now the LORD says, ‘Far be it from me;
for those who honour me I will honour,

386
00:28:59,093 --> 00:29:01,333
and those who despise me will be cursed.

387
00:29:02,053 --> 00:29:07,973
Behold, the days come that I will cut off
your arm and the arm of your father’s house,

388
00:29:08,793 --> 00:29:11,813
that there will not be an old man in your
house.

389
00:29:12,120 --> 00:29:18,240
You will see the affliction of my habitation,
in all the wealth which I will give Israel.

390
00:29:19,380 --> 00:29:22,420
There shall not be an old man in your
house forever.

391
00:29:23,420 --> 00:29:29,440
The man of yours whom I don’t cut off from
my altar will consume your eyes and grieve

392
00:29:29,480 --> 00:29:30,380
your heart.

393
00:29:30,740 --> 00:29:34,440
All the increase of your house will die in
the flower of their age.

394
00:29:35,400 --> 00:29:41,580
This will be the sign to you that will
come on your two sons, on Hophni and Phinehas:

395
00:29:41,620 --> 00:29:43,520
in one day they will both die.

396
00:29:43,980 --> 00:29:49,360
I will raise up a faithful priest for myself
who will do according to that which is in

397
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:50,960
my heart and in my mind.

398
00:29:51,460 --> 00:29:53,160
I will build him a sure house.

399
00:29:53,940 --> 00:29:56,220
He will walk before my anointed forever.

400
00:29:56,940 --> 00:30:02,200
It will happen that everyone who is left in
your house will come and bow down to him

401
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:08,760
for a piece of silver and a loaf of bread,
and will say, “Please put me into one of

402
00:30:08,800 --> 00:30:15,440
the priests’ offices, that I may eat
a morsel of bread.”’” First Samuel, chapter three.

403
00:30:15,480 --> 00:30:18,800
The child Samuel ministered to the LORD
before Eli.

404
00:30:19,820 --> 00:30:22,300
The LORD’s word was rare in those days.

405
00:30:23,240 --> 00:30:24,900
There were not many visions, then.

406
00:30:25,420 --> 00:30:32,000
At that time, when Eli was laid down in
his place (now his eyes had begun to grow

407
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:38,920
dim, so that he could not see), and God’s
lamp hadn’t yet gone out, and Samuel

408
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:44,480
had laid down in the LORD’s temple where
God’s ark was, The LORD called Samuel.

409
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:47,220
He said, “Here I am.”

410
00:30:48,080 --> 00:30:52,980
He ran to Eli and said, “Here I am; for
you called me.”

411
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:55,380
He said, “I didn’t call.

412
00:30:55,420 --> 00:30:56,940
Lie down again.”

413
00:30:57,900 --> 00:30:59,120
He went and lay down.

414
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:02,780
The LORD called yet again, “Samuel!”

415
00:31:03,140 --> 00:31:08,840
Samuel arose and went to Eli and said,
“Here I am; for you called me.”

416
00:31:09,680 --> 00:31:12,320
He answered, “I didn’t call, my son.

417
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:13,900
Lie down again.”

418
00:31:14,600 --> 00:31:20,280
Now Samuel didn’t yet know the LORD, neither
was the LORD’s word yet revealed to him.

419
00:31:21,080 --> 00:31:23,880
The LORD called Samuel again the third
time.

420
00:31:24,840 --> 00:31:30,200
He arose and went to Eli and said, “Here I
am; for you called me.”

421
00:31:30,580 --> 00:31:33,260
Eli perceived that the LORD had called the
child.

422
00:31:34,120 --> 00:31:38,220
Therefore Eli said to Samuel, “Go, lie
down.

423
00:31:38,614 --> 00:31:45,114
It shall be, if he calls you, that you
shall say, ‘Speak, LORD; for your

424
00:31:45,154 --> 00:31:50,094
servant hears.’” So Samuel went and lay
down in his place.

425
00:31:51,114 --> 00:31:56,514
The LORD came, and stood, and called as at
other times, “Samuel!

426
00:31:57,274 --> 00:31:58,174
Samuel!”

427
00:31:58,794 --> 00:32:02,734
Then Samuel said, “Speak; for your servant
hears.”

428
00:32:03,294 --> 00:32:09,774
The LORD said to Samuel, “Behold, I will do
a thing in Israel at which both the ears

429
00:32:09,814 --> 00:32:11,954
of everyone who hears it will tingle.

430
00:32:13,054 --> 00:32:19,154
In that day I will perform against Eli
all that I have spoken concerning his house, from

431
00:32:19,194 --> 00:32:20,814
the beginning even to the end.

432
00:32:21,414 --> 00:32:26,394
For I have told him that I will judge
his house forever for the iniquity which he knew,

433
00:32:26,994 --> 00:32:31,274
because his sons brought a curse on
themselves, and he didn’t restrain them.

434
00:32:31,874 --> 00:32:38,194
Therefore I have sworn to the house of Eli
that the iniquity of Eli’s house shall not

435
00:32:38,234 --> 00:32:41,434
be removed with sacrifice or offering
forever.”

436
00:32:42,754 --> 00:32:47,574
Samuel lay until the morning, and opened
the doors of the LORD’s house.

437
00:32:48,594 --> 00:32:51,554
Samuel was afraid to show Eli the vision.

438
00:32:52,114 --> 00:32:56,874
Then Eli called Samuel and said, “Samuel,
my son!”

439
00:32:57,594 --> 00:32:59,234
He said, “Here I am.”

440
00:33:00,054 --> 00:33:03,414
He said, “What is the thing that he has
spoken to you?

441
00:33:04,074 --> 00:33:05,714
Please don’t hide it from me.

442
00:33:06,394 --> 00:33:12,914
God do so to you, and more also, if
you hide anything from me of all the things that

443
00:33:12,954 --> 00:33:13,874
he spoke to you.”

444
00:33:14,874 --> 00:33:17,954
Samuel told him every bit, and hid nothing
from him.

445
00:33:19,014 --> 00:33:21,014
He said, “It is the LORD.

446
00:33:21,734 --> 00:33:23,814
Let him do what seems good to him.”

447
00:33:24,874 --> 00:33:30,454
Samuel grew, and the LORD was with him and
let none of his words fall to the ground.

448
00:33:31,254 --> 00:33:37,394
All Israel from Dan even to Beersheba knew
that Samuel was established to be a prophet

449
00:33:37,434 --> 00:33:38,334
of the LORD.

450
00:33:38,914 --> 00:33:45,334
The LORD appeared again in Shiloh; for the
LORD revealed himself to Samuel in Shiloh

451
00:33:45,374 --> 00:33:46,494
by the LORD’s word.

452
00:33:46,534 --> 00:33:50,154
First Samuel, chapter four.

453
00:33:50,194 --> 00:33:52,654
The word of Samuel came to all Israel.

454
00:33:53,614 --> 00:33:59,294
Now Israel went out against the
Philistines to battle, and encamped beside Ebenezer;

455
00:34:00,274 --> 00:34:03,474
and the Philistines encamped in Aphek.

456
00:34:03,514 --> 00:34:06,714
The Philistines put themselves in array
against Israel.

457
00:34:07,104 --> 00:34:13,244
When they joined battle, Israel was defeated
by the Philistines, who killed about four

458
00:34:13,284 --> 00:34:15,484
thousand men of the army in the field.

459
00:34:16,364 --> 00:34:22,864
When the people had come into the camp,
the elders of Israel said, “Why has the LORD

460
00:34:22,904 --> 00:34:25,744
defeated us today before the Philistines?

461
00:34:26,404 --> 00:34:32,184
Let’s get the ark of the LORD’s covenant out
of Shiloh and bring it to us, that it may

462
00:34:32,224 --> 00:34:36,004
come amongst us and save us out of the
hand of our enemies.”

463
00:34:37,144 --> 00:34:42,744
So the people sent to Shiloh, and they
brought from there the ark of the covenant of

464
00:34:42,784 --> 00:34:49,464
the LORD of Armies, who sits above the
cherubim; and the two sons of Eli, Hophni and

465
00:34:49,504 --> 00:34:52,764
Phinehas, were there with the ark of the
covenant of God.

466
00:34:53,804 --> 00:34:59,504
When the ark of the LORD’s covenant came
into the camp, all Israel shouted with a great

467
00:34:59,544 --> 00:35:01,724
shout, so that the earth resounded.

468
00:35:02,464 --> 00:35:08,084
When the Philistines heard the noise of the
shout, they said, “What does the noise of

469
00:35:08,124 --> 00:35:10,844
this great shout in the camp of the
Hebrews mean?”

470
00:35:11,864 --> 00:35:15,304
They understood that the LORD’s ark had
come into the camp.

471
00:35:16,164 --> 00:35:21,264
The Philistines were afraid, for they
said, “God has come into the camp.”

472
00:35:21,744 --> 00:35:23,604
They said, “Woe to us!

473
00:35:24,164 --> 00:35:26,324
For there has not been such a thing
before.

474
00:35:27,304 --> 00:35:28,204
Woe to us!

475
00:35:28,584 --> 00:35:31,724
Who shall deliver us out of the hand of
these mighty gods?

476
00:35:32,364 --> 00:35:37,644
These are the gods that struck the Egyptians
with all kinds of plagues in the wilderness.

477
00:35:38,544 --> 00:35:45,024
Be strong and behave like men, O you
Philistines, that you not be servants to

478
00:35:45,064 --> 00:35:47,484
the Hebrews, as they have been to you.

479
00:35:48,604 --> 00:35:51,564
Strengthen yourselves like men, and
fight!”

480
00:35:52,644 --> 00:35:58,544
The Philistines fought, and Israel was
defeated, and each man fled to his tent.

481
00:35:59,664 --> 00:36:04,764
There was a very great slaughter; for
thirty thousand footmen of Israel fell.

482
00:36:05,864 --> 00:36:12,324
God’s ark was taken; and the two sons of
Eli, Hophni and Phinehas, were

483
00:36:12,364 --> 00:36:13,264
slain.

484
00:36:14,004 --> 00:36:20,364
A man of Benjamin ran out of the army
and came to Shiloh the same day, with his clothes

485
00:36:20,404 --> 00:36:22,824
torn and with dirt on his head.

486
00:36:23,484 --> 00:36:30,144
When he came, behold, Eli was sitting on
his seat by the road watching, for

487
00:36:30,184 --> 00:36:32,024
his heart trembled for God’s ark.

488
00:36:32,683 --> 00:36:37,963
When the man came into the city and told
about it, all the city cried out.

489
00:36:38,983 --> 00:36:44,803
When Eli heard the noise of the crying, he
said, “What does the noise of this tumult

490
00:36:44,843 --> 00:36:45,743
mean?”

491
00:36:46,483 --> 00:36:49,223
The man hurried, and came and told Eli.

492
00:36:50,463 --> 00:36:52,983
Now Eli was ninety-eight years old.

493
00:36:53,983 --> 00:36:56,903
His eyes were set, so that he could not
see.

494
00:36:57,623 --> 00:37:04,123
The man said to Eli, “I am he who came out
of the army, and I fled today out of the

495
00:37:04,163 --> 00:37:05,063
army.”

496
00:37:05,403 --> 00:37:08,483
He said, “How did the matter go, my son?”

497
00:37:09,623 --> 00:37:15,603
He who brought the news answered, “Israel
has fled before the Philistines, and there

498
00:37:15,643 --> 00:37:18,663
has been also a great slaughter amongst
the people.

499
00:37:19,323 --> 00:37:25,683
Your two sons also, Hophni and Phinehas,
are dead, and God’s ark has been captured.”

500
00:37:26,603 --> 00:37:32,883
When he made mention of God’s ark, Eli fell
from off his seat backward by the side of

501
00:37:32,923 --> 00:37:38,703
the gate; and his neck broke, and he died,
for he was an old man and heavy.

502
00:37:39,563 --> 00:37:41,763
He had judged Israel forty years.

503
00:37:42,403 --> 00:37:47,483
His daughter-in-law, Phinehas’ wife, was
with child, near to giving birth.

504
00:37:48,503 --> 00:37:54,403
When she heard the news that God’s ark
was taken and that her father-in-law and her husband

505
00:37:54,443 --> 00:38:00,003
were dead, she bowed herself and gave
birth; for her pains came on her.

506
00:38:00,803 --> 00:38:06,143
About the time of her death the women who
stood by her said to her, “Don’t be afraid,

507
00:38:06,943 --> 00:38:08,783
for you have given birth to a son.”

508
00:38:09,623 --> 00:38:12,943
But she didn’t answer, neither did she
regard it.

509
00:38:13,843 --> 00:38:18,823
She named the child Ichabod, saying, “The
glory has departed from Israel!”

510
00:38:18,863 --> 00:38:24,543
because God’s ark was taken, and because
of her father-in-law and her husband.

511
00:38:25,623 --> 00:38:31,463
She said, “The glory has departed from
Israel; for God’s ark has been taken.”

512
00:38:31,503 --> 00:38:36,103
First Samuel, chapter five.

513
00:38:36,143 --> 00:38:41,903
Now the Philistines had taken God’s ark,
and they brought it from Ebenezer to Ashdod.

514
00:38:42,583 --> 00:38:48,083
The Philistines took God’s ark, and brought it
into the house of Dagon and set it by

515
00:38:48,123 --> 00:38:49,023
Dagon.

516
00:38:49,403 --> 00:38:56,003
When the people of Ashdod arose early on
the next day, behold, Dagon had fallen on

517
00:38:56,043 --> 00:38:58,523
his face to the ground before the LORD’s
ark.

518
00:38:59,483 --> 00:39:02,423
They took Dagon and set him in his place
again.

519
00:39:02,838 --> 00:39:09,498
When they arose early on the following
morning, behold, Dagon had fallen on his face

520
00:39:09,538 --> 00:39:15,838
to the ground before the LORD’s ark; and the
head of Dagon and both the palms of his

521
00:39:15,878 --> 00:39:17,658
hands were cut off on the threshold.

522
00:39:18,698 --> 00:39:21,118
Only Dagon’s torso was intact.

523
00:39:21,838 --> 00:39:28,118
Therefore neither the priests of Dagon nor any
who come into Dagon’s house step on the

524
00:39:28,158 --> 00:39:31,158
threshold of Dagon in Ashdod to this day.

525
00:39:32,038 --> 00:39:38,138
But the LORD’s hand was heavy on the
people of Ashdod, and he destroyed them and struck

526
00:39:38,178 --> 00:39:41,498
them with tumours, even Ashdod and its
borders.

527
00:39:42,438 --> 00:39:48,878
When the men of Ashdod saw that it was so,
they said, “The ark of the God of Israel shall

528
00:39:48,918 --> 00:39:54,378
not stay with us, for his hand is severe
on us and on Dagon our god.”

529
00:39:54,858 --> 00:40:00,818
They sent therefore and gathered together all
the lords of the Philistines, and said,

530
00:40:01,898 --> 00:40:04,518
“What shall we do with the ark of the God
of Israel?”

531
00:40:05,318 --> 00:40:10,578
They answered, “Let the ark of the God of
Israel be carried over to Gath.”

532
00:40:11,238 --> 00:40:14,218
They carried the ark of the God of Israel
there.

533
00:40:14,978 --> 00:40:20,618
It was so, that after they had carried
it there, the LORD’s hand was against the city

534
00:40:20,658 --> 00:40:26,918
with a very great confusion; and he struck
the men of the city, both small and great,

535
00:40:27,518 --> 00:40:29,478
so that tumours broke out on them.

536
00:40:30,278 --> 00:40:32,898
So they sent God’s ark to Ekron.

537
00:40:32,938 --> 00:40:39,498
As God’s ark came to Ekron, the Ekronites
cried out, saying, “They have

538
00:40:39,538 --> 00:40:44,678
brought the ark of the God of Israel here
to us, to kill us and our people.”

539
00:40:45,238 --> 00:40:51,198
They sent therefore and gathered together
all the lords of the Philistines, and they

540
00:40:51,238 --> 00:40:57,758
said, “Send the ark of the God of Israel
away, and let it go again to its own place,

541
00:40:58,698 --> 00:41:00,638
that it not kill us and our people.”

542
00:41:01,038 --> 00:41:03,718
For there was a deadly panic throughout
all the city.

543
00:41:04,298 --> 00:41:06,438
The hand of God was very heavy there.

544
00:41:07,358 --> 00:41:12,638
The men who didn’t die were struck with the
tumours; and the cry of the city went up

545
00:41:12,678 --> 00:41:13,078
to heaven.

546
00:41:13,118 --> 00:41:16,858
First Samuel, chapter six.

547
00:41:16,898 --> 00:41:21,158
The LORD’s ark was in the country of the
Philistines seven months.

548
00:41:21,595 --> 00:41:27,835
The Philistines called for the priests and
the diviners, saying, “What shall we do with

549
00:41:27,875 --> 00:41:28,895
the LORD’s ark?

550
00:41:29,635 --> 00:41:32,075
Show us how we should send it to its
place.”

551
00:41:33,055 --> 00:41:39,955
They said, “If you send away the ark of
the God of Israel, don’t send it empty; but

552
00:41:39,995 --> 00:41:43,175
by all means return a trespass offering to
him.

553
00:41:43,795 --> 00:41:49,435
Then you will be healed, and it will be
known to you why his hand is not removed from

554
00:41:49,475 --> 00:41:50,375
you.”

555
00:41:50,515 --> 00:41:56,215
Then they said, “What should the trespass
offering be which we shall return to him?”

556
00:41:57,315 --> 00:42:03,695
They said, “Five golden tumours and five golden
mice, for the number of the lords of

557
00:42:03,735 --> 00:42:08,575
the Philistines; for one plague was on you
all, and on your lords.

558
00:42:09,575 --> 00:42:15,075
Therefore you shall make images of your tumours
and images of your mice that mar the

559
00:42:15,115 --> 00:42:18,795
land; and you shall give glory to the God
of Israel.

560
00:42:19,875 --> 00:42:25,035
Perhaps he will release his hand from you,
from your gods, and from your land.

561
00:42:25,755 --> 00:42:30,475
Why then do you harden your hearts
as the Egyptians and Pharaoh hardened their hearts?

562
00:42:31,635 --> 00:42:36,815
When he had worked wonderfully amongst them,
didn’t they let the people go, and they

563
00:42:36,855 --> 00:42:37,755
departed?

564
00:42:38,155 --> 00:42:44,295
“Now therefore take and prepare yourselves a new
cart and two milk cows on which there

565
00:42:44,335 --> 00:42:50,115
has come no yoke; and tie the cows to
the cart, and bring their calves home from them;

566
00:42:50,835 --> 00:42:53,395
and take the LORD’s ark and lay it on the
cart.

567
00:42:54,315 --> 00:43:00,295
Put the jewels of gold, which you return him
for a trespass offering, in a box by its

568
00:43:00,335 --> 00:43:03,635
side; and send it away, that it may go.

569
00:43:04,295 --> 00:43:10,795
Behold, if it goes up by the way of
its own border to Beth Shemesh, then he has done

570
00:43:10,835 --> 00:43:17,075
us this great evil; but if not, then we
shall know that it is not his hand that struck

571
00:43:17,115 --> 00:43:18,015
us.

572
00:43:18,155 --> 00:43:20,295
It was a chance that happened to us.”

573
00:43:20,775 --> 00:43:27,075
The men did so, and took two milk cows and
tied them to the cart, and shut up their calves

574
00:43:27,115 --> 00:43:28,015
at home.

575
00:43:28,695 --> 00:43:34,055
They put the LORD’s ark on the cart, and
the box with the golden mice and the images

576
00:43:34,095 --> 00:43:35,815
of their tumours.

577
00:43:35,855 --> 00:43:39,575
The cows took the straight way by the way
to Beth Shemesh.

578
00:43:39,919 --> 00:43:46,319
They went along the highway, lowing as they
went, and didn’t turn away to the right hand

579
00:43:46,359 --> 00:43:52,439
or to the left; and the lords of the
Philistines went after them to the border of Beth

580
00:43:52,479 --> 00:43:53,379
Shemesh.

581
00:43:53,779 --> 00:43:59,099
The people of Beth Shemesh were reaping their
wheat harvest in the valley; and they lifted

582
00:43:59,139 --> 00:44:03,359
up their eyes and saw the ark, and
rejoiced to see it.

583
00:44:03,999 --> 00:44:10,399
The cart came into the field of Joshua of
Beth Shemesh, and stood there, where there

584
00:44:10,439 --> 00:44:11,439
was a great stone.

585
00:44:12,459 --> 00:44:18,139
Then they split the wood of the cart and
offered up the cows for a burnt offering to

586
00:44:18,179 --> 00:44:19,079
the LORD.

587
00:44:19,339 --> 00:44:24,699
The Levites took down the LORD’s ark and the
box that was with it, in which the jewels

588
00:44:24,739 --> 00:44:31,299
of gold were, and put them on the great
stone; and the men of Beth Shemesh offered burnt

589
00:44:31,339 --> 00:44:36,159
offerings and sacrificed sacrifices the
same day to the LORD.

590
00:44:36,759 --> 00:44:42,659
When the five lords of the Philistines had
seen it, they returned to Ekron the same day.

591
00:44:43,459 --> 00:44:49,059
These are the golden tumours which the
Philistines returned for a trespass offering to

592
00:44:49,099 --> 00:44:56,059
the LORD: for Ashdod one, for Gaza one,
for Ashkelon one,

593
00:44:56,099 --> 00:45:02,639
for Gath one, for Ekron one; and the
golden mice, according to the number of all the

594
00:45:02,679 --> 00:45:08,959
cities of the Philistines belonging to the
five lords, both of fortified cities and of

595
00:45:08,999 --> 00:45:14,699
country villages, even to the great stone
on which they set down the LORD’s ark.

596
00:45:15,359 --> 00:45:20,279
That stone remains to this day in the
field of Joshua of Beth Shemesh.

597
00:45:20,859 --> 00:45:27,399
He struck of the men of Beth Shemesh,
because they had looked into the LORD’s ark, he

598
00:45:27,439 --> 00:45:30,239
struck fifty thousand and seventy of the
men.

599
00:45:30,899 --> 00:45:35,859
Then the people mourned, because the LORD
had struck the people with a great slaughter.

600
00:45:36,639 --> 00:45:42,879
The men of Beth Shemesh said, “Who is able
to stand before the LORD, this holy God?

601
00:45:43,639 --> 00:45:45,719
To whom shall he go up from us?”

602
00:45:46,619 --> 00:45:53,039
They sent messengers to the inhabitants
of Kiriath Jearim, saying, “The Philistines have

603
00:45:53,079 --> 00:45:54,779
brought back the LORD’s ark.

604
00:45:55,579 --> 00:45:57,319
Come down and bring it up to yourselves.”

605
00:45:57,359 --> 00:45:59,899
First Samuel, chapter seven.

606
00:46:00,873 --> 00:46:07,313
The men of Kiriath Jearim came and took
the LORD’s ark, and brought it into Abinadab’s

607
00:46:07,353 --> 00:46:13,293
house on the hill, and consecrated Eleazar
his son to keep the LORD’s ark.

608
00:46:14,453 --> 00:46:20,493
From the day that the ark stayed in
Kiriath Jearim, the time was long—for it was twenty

609
00:46:20,533 --> 00:46:25,113
years; and all the house of Israel
lamented after the LORD.

610
00:46:26,053 --> 00:46:32,493
Samuel spoke to all the house of Israel,
saying, “If you are returning to the LORD with

611
00:46:32,533 --> 00:46:39,013
all your heart, then put away the foreign
gods and the Ashtaroth from amongst you, and

612
00:46:39,053 --> 00:46:44,693
direct your hearts to the LORD, and serve him
only; and he will deliver you out of the

613
00:46:44,733 --> 00:46:46,013
hand of the Philistines.”

614
00:46:47,153 --> 00:46:52,893
Then the children of Israel removed the
Baals and the Ashtaroth, and served the LORD

615
00:46:52,933 --> 00:46:53,833
only.

616
00:46:54,353 --> 00:47:00,573
Samuel said, “Gather all Israel to Mizpah,
and I will pray to the LORD for you.”

617
00:47:01,093 --> 00:47:06,553
They gathered together to Mizpah, and drew
water, and poured it out before the LORD,

618
00:47:07,273 --> 00:47:12,733
and fasted on that day, and said there,
“We have sinned against the LORD.”

619
00:47:13,673 --> 00:47:16,753
Samuel judged the children of Israel in
Mizpah.

620
00:47:16,793 --> 00:47:22,573
When the Philistines heard that the children
of Israel were gathered together at Mizpah,

621
00:47:22,613 --> 00:47:25,433
the lords of the Philistines went up
against Israel.

622
00:47:26,433 --> 00:47:30,573
When the children of Israel heard it, they
were afraid of the Philistines.

623
00:47:31,333 --> 00:47:37,293
The children of Israel said to Samuel, “Don’t
stop crying to the LORD our God for us,

624
00:47:37,933 --> 00:47:40,953
that he will save us out of the hand of
the Philistines.”

625
00:47:42,053 --> 00:47:48,053
Samuel took a suckling lamb, and offered
it for a whole burnt offering to the LORD.

626
00:47:48,873 --> 00:47:53,353
Samuel cried to the LORD for Israel, and
the LORD answered him.

627
00:47:53,873 --> 00:47:59,733
As Samuel was offering up the burnt
offering, the Philistines came near to battle against

628
00:47:59,773 --> 00:48:05,913
Israel; but the LORD thundered with a great
thunder on that day on the Philistines and

629
00:48:05,953 --> 00:48:09,473
confused them; and they were struck down
before Israel.

630
00:48:10,273 --> 00:48:16,273
The men of Israel went out of Mizpah
and pursued the Philistines, and struck them until

631
00:48:16,313 --> 00:48:17,333
they came under Beth Kar.

632
00:48:18,159 --> 00:48:24,779
Then Samuel took a stone and set it
between Mizpah and Shen, and called its name

633
00:48:24,819 --> 00:48:29,839
Ebenezer, saying, “The LORD helped us
until now.”

634
00:48:29,879 --> 00:48:35,879
So the Philistines were subdued, and they
stopped coming within the border of Israel.

635
00:48:36,419 --> 00:48:40,159
The LORD’s hand was against the
Philistines all the days of Samuel.

636
00:48:40,739 --> 00:48:46,799
The cities which the Philistines had taken
from Israel were restored to Israel, from

637
00:48:46,839 --> 00:48:53,599
Ekron even to Gath; and Israel recovered its
border out of the hand of the Philistines.

638
00:48:54,579 --> 00:48:57,559
There was peace between Israel and the
Amorites.

639
00:48:57,859 --> 00:49:01,179
Samuel judged Israel all the days of his
life.

640
00:49:01,859 --> 00:49:08,739
He went from year to year in a circuit
to Bethel, Gilgal, and Mizpah; and he judged Israel

641
00:49:08,779 --> 00:49:10,049
in all those places.

642
00:49:11,389 --> 00:49:18,169
His return was to Ramah, for his house was
there, and he judged Israel there; and

643
00:49:18,209 --> 00:49:20,149
he built an altar to the LORD there.

644
00:49:20,189 --> 00:49:23,369
First Samuel, chapter eight.

645
00:49:23,409 --> 00:49:27,729
When Samuel was old, he made his sons
judges over Israel.

646
00:49:28,969 --> 00:49:34,909
Now the name of his firstborn was Joel,
and the name of his second, Abijah.

647
00:49:34,949 --> 00:49:37,089
They were judges in Beersheba.

648
00:49:37,129 --> 00:49:43,849
His sons didn’t walk in his ways, but
turned away after dishonest gain, took

649
00:49:43,889 --> 00:49:46,009
bribes, and perverted justice.

650
00:49:47,029 --> 00:49:53,489
Then all the elders of Israel gathered
themselves together and came to Samuel to Ramah.

651
00:49:53,529 --> 00:49:59,529
They said to him, “Behold, you are old,
and your sons don’t walk in your ways.

652
00:50:00,389 --> 00:50:03,429
Now make us a king to judge us like all
the nations.”

653
00:50:04,129 --> 00:50:09,369
But the thing displeased Samuel when they
said, “Give us a king to judge us.”

654
00:50:10,449 --> 00:50:12,129
Samuel prayed to the LORD.

655
00:50:12,769 --> 00:50:19,149
The LORD said to Samuel, “Listen to the voice
of the people in all that they tell you;

656
00:50:19,849 --> 00:50:25,069
for they have not rejected you, but they
have rejected me as the king over them.

657
00:50:25,549 --> 00:50:29,889
According to all the works which they have
done since the day that I brought them up

658
00:50:29,929 --> 00:50:36,969
out of Egypt even to this day, in that
they have forsaken me and served other gods, so

659
00:50:37,009 --> 00:50:38,469
they also do to you.

660
00:50:39,349 --> 00:50:41,709
Now therefore, listen to their voice.

661
00:50:42,160 --> 00:50:48,240
However, you shall protest solemnly to them, and
shall show them the way of the king

662
00:50:48,280 --> 00:50:49,780
who will reign over them.”

663
00:50:50,920 --> 00:50:55,500
Samuel told all the LORD’s words to the
people who asked him for a king.

664
00:50:56,140 --> 00:51:02,340
He said, “This will be the way of the
king who shall reign over you: he will take your

665
00:51:02,380 --> 00:51:09,220
sons and appoint them as his servants, for
his chariots and to be his horsemen; and

666
00:51:09,260 --> 00:51:11,160
they will run before his chariots.

667
00:51:11,200 --> 00:51:17,360
He will appoint them to him for captains
of thousands and captains of fifties; and he

668
00:51:17,400 --> 00:51:23,120
will assign some to plough his ground and
to reap his harvest; and to make his instruments

669
00:51:23,160 --> 00:51:26,200
of war and the instruments of his
chariots.

670
00:51:27,100 --> 00:51:32,200
He will take your daughters to be
perfumers, to be cooks, and to be bakers.

671
00:51:32,980 --> 00:51:39,440
He will take your fields, your vineyards,
and your olive groves, even your best, and

672
00:51:39,480 --> 00:51:40,720
give them to his servants.

673
00:51:42,100 --> 00:51:47,780
He will take one tenth of your seed and
of your vineyards, and give it to his officers

674
00:51:47,820 --> 00:51:49,360
and to his servants.

675
00:51:50,140 --> 00:51:56,240
He will take your male servants, your
female servants, your best young men, and your

676
00:51:56,280 --> 00:51:59,340
donkeys, and assign them to his own work.

677
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:04,600
He will take one tenth of your flocks; and
you will be his servants.

678
00:52:05,680 --> 00:52:10,880
You will cry out in that day because of
your king whom you will have chosen for yourselves;

679
00:52:11,700 --> 00:52:14,200
and the LORD will not answer you in that
day.”

680
00:52:15,220 --> 00:52:22,340
But the people refused to listen to the
voice of Samuel; and they said, “No, but

681
00:52:22,380 --> 00:52:28,680
we will have a king over us, that we also
may be like all the nations; and that our king

682
00:52:28,720 --> 00:52:32,980
may judge us, and go out before us, and
fight our battles.”

683
00:52:33,780 --> 00:52:39,160
Samuel heard all the words of the people, and
he rehearsed them in the ears of the LORD.

684
00:52:40,180 --> 00:52:44,880
The LORD said to Samuel, “Listen to their
voice, and make them a king.”

685
00:52:45,440 --> 00:52:49,740
Samuel said to the men of Israel,
“Everyone go to your own city.”

686
00:52:49,780 --> 00:52:52,300
First Samuel, chapter nine.

687
00:52:53,142 --> 00:52:59,622
Now there was a man of Benjamin, whose
name was Kish the son of Abiel, the son

688
00:52:59,662 --> 00:53:06,642
of Zeror, the son of Becorath, the son of
Aphiah, the son of a Benjamite,

689
00:53:06,682 --> 00:53:09,002
a mighty man of valour.

690
00:53:09,042 --> 00:53:15,442
He had a son whose name was Saul,
an impressive young man; and there was not amongst

691
00:53:15,482 --> 00:53:19,102
the children of Israel a more handsome
person than he.

692
00:53:19,962 --> 00:53:24,082
From his shoulders and upward he was
taller than any of the people.

693
00:53:25,062 --> 00:53:28,162
The donkeys of Kish, Saul’s father, were
lost.

694
00:53:28,902 --> 00:53:35,422
Kish said to Saul his son, “Now take one
of the servants with you, and arise, go

695
00:53:35,462 --> 00:53:36,502
look for the donkeys.”

696
00:53:37,342 --> 00:53:42,922
He passed through the hill country of
Ephraim, and passed through the land of Shalishah,

697
00:53:42,962 --> 00:53:44,242
but they didn’t find them.

698
00:53:45,002 --> 00:53:48,582
Then they passed through the land of
Shaalim, and they weren’t there.

699
00:53:49,222 --> 00:53:53,702
Then he passed through the land of the
Benjamites, but they didn’t find them.

700
00:53:54,662 --> 00:54:00,782
When they had come to the land of Zuph,
Saul said to his servant who was with him, “Come!

701
00:54:01,522 --> 00:54:07,482
Let’s return, lest my father stop caring
about the donkeys and be anxious for us.”

702
00:54:08,102 --> 00:54:14,582
The servant said to him, “Behold now, there is a
man of God in this city, and he is a

703
00:54:14,622 --> 00:54:17,022
man who is held in honour.

704
00:54:17,062 --> 00:54:19,242
All that he says surely happens.

705
00:54:19,962 --> 00:54:21,102
Now let’s go there.

706
00:54:21,782 --> 00:54:23,942
Perhaps he can tell us which way to go.”

707
00:54:24,602 --> 00:54:31,122
Then Saul said to his servant, “But
behold, if we go, what should we bring the

708
00:54:31,162 --> 00:54:32,062
man?

709
00:54:32,142 --> 00:54:37,542
For the bread is spent in our sacks, and there
is not a present to bring to the man of

710
00:54:37,582 --> 00:54:38,482
God.

711
00:54:38,702 --> 00:54:39,662
What do we have?”

712
00:54:40,282 --> 00:54:46,902
The servant answered Saul again and said,
“Behold, I have in my hand the fourth part

713
00:54:46,942 --> 00:54:48,122
of a shekel of silver.

714
00:54:48,882 --> 00:54:52,902
I will give that to the man of God, to
tell us our way.”

715
00:54:52,942 --> 00:54:59,622
(In earlier times in Israel, when a man
went to enquire of God, he said, “Come!

716
00:55:00,182 --> 00:55:06,542
Let’s go to the seer;” for he who is
now called a prophet was before called a seer.)

717
00:55:06,982 --> 00:55:09,722
Then Saul said to his servant, “Well said.

718
00:55:10,442 --> 00:55:11,142
Come!

719
00:55:11,182 --> 00:55:12,082
Let’s go.”

720
00:55:12,662 --> 00:55:15,902
So they went to the city where the man of
God was.

721
00:55:16,312 --> 00:55:22,172
As they went up the ascent to the city,
they found young maidens going out to draw water,

722
00:55:22,752 --> 00:55:25,792
and said to them, “Is the seer here?”

723
00:55:26,352 --> 00:55:29,052
They answered them and said, “He is.

724
00:55:29,592 --> 00:55:31,572
Behold, he is before you.

725
00:55:32,272 --> 00:55:38,132
Hurry now, for he has come today into
the city; for the people have a sacrifice today

726
00:55:38,172 --> 00:55:39,292
in the high place.

727
00:55:40,152 --> 00:55:45,472
As soon as you have come into the
city, you will immediately find him before he goes

728
00:55:45,512 --> 00:55:52,252
up to the high place to eat; for the
people will not eat until he comes, because he blesses

729
00:55:52,292 --> 00:55:53,192
the sacrifice.

730
00:55:54,052 --> 00:55:56,332
Afterwards those who are invited eat.

731
00:55:56,832 --> 00:56:00,532
Now therefore go up; for at this time you
will find him.”

732
00:56:01,452 --> 00:56:02,992
They went up to the city.

733
00:56:03,872 --> 00:56:10,132
As they came within the city, behold, Samuel came
out towards them to go up to the high

734
00:56:10,172 --> 00:56:11,052
place.

735
00:56:11,092 --> 00:56:17,632
Now the LORD had revealed to Samuel a day
before Saul came, saying, “Tomorrow

736
00:56:17,672 --> 00:56:23,612
about this time I will send you a man
out of the land of Benjamin, and you shall anoint

737
00:56:23,652 --> 00:56:26,092
him to be prince over my people Israel.

738
00:56:27,012 --> 00:56:32,372
He will save my people out of the hand of
the Philistines; for I have looked upon my

739
00:56:32,412 --> 00:56:35,332
people, because their cry has come to me.”

740
00:56:36,392 --> 00:56:42,872
When Samuel saw Saul, the LORD said to
him, “Behold, the man of whom I spoke to

741
00:56:42,912 --> 00:56:43,812
you!

742
00:56:43,852 --> 00:56:46,012
He will have authority over my people.”

743
00:56:46,652 --> 00:56:52,932
Then Saul approached Samuel in the gateway,
and said, “Please tell me where the seer’s

744
00:56:52,972 --> 00:56:53,872
house is.”

745
00:56:54,512 --> 00:56:58,252
Samuel answered Saul and said, “I am the
seer.

746
00:56:58,932 --> 00:57:03,332
Go up before me to the high place, for you
are to eat with me today.

747
00:57:04,032 --> 00:57:08,472
In the morning I will let you go and will
tell you all that is in your heart.

748
00:57:09,512 --> 00:57:15,532
As for your donkeys who were lost three days
ago, don’t set your mind on them, for they

749
00:57:15,572 --> 00:57:16,472
have been found.

750
00:57:16,732 --> 00:57:18,872
For whom does all Israel desire?

751
00:57:19,652 --> 00:57:22,892
Is it not you and all your father’s
house?”

752
00:57:23,692 --> 00:57:29,132
Saul answered, “Am I not a Benjamite, of
the smallest of the tribes of Israel?

753
00:57:29,632 --> 00:57:33,812
And my family the least of all the
families of the tribe of Benjamin?

754
00:57:34,712 --> 00:57:37,092
Why then do you speak to me like this?”

755
00:57:37,525 --> 00:57:43,325
Samuel took Saul and his servant and brought
them into the guest room, and made them

756
00:57:43,365 --> 00:57:49,025
sit in the best place amongst those
who were invited, who were about thirty persons.

757
00:57:50,345 --> 00:57:56,785
Samuel said to the cook, “Bring the portion which
I gave you, of which I said to you,

758
00:57:57,605 --> 00:58:03,765
‘Set it aside.’” The cook took up the thigh,
and that which was on it, and set it before

759
00:58:03,805 --> 00:58:04,705
Saul.

760
00:58:05,125 --> 00:58:09,485
Samuel said, “Behold, that which has been
reserved!

761
00:58:10,485 --> 00:58:16,265
Set it before yourself and eat; because it
has been kept for you for the appointed time,

762
00:58:17,085 --> 00:58:22,725
for I said, ‘I have invited the people.’”
So Saul ate with Samuel that day.

763
00:58:23,605 --> 00:58:28,805
When they had come down from the high place
into the city, he talked with Saul on the

764
00:58:28,845 --> 00:58:29,745
housetop.

765
00:58:30,145 --> 00:58:36,825
They arose early; and about daybreak, Samuel
called to Saul on the housetop, saying,

766
00:58:37,585 --> 00:58:39,785
“Get up, that I may send you away.”

767
00:58:40,385 --> 00:58:45,405
Saul arose, and they both went outside, he
and Samuel, together.

768
00:58:46,505 --> 00:58:52,885
As they were going down at the end of
the city, Samuel said to Saul, “Tell the servant

769
00:58:52,925 --> 00:58:54,525
to go on ahead of us.”

770
00:58:54,725 --> 00:59:01,325
He went ahead, then Samuel said, “But
stand still first, that I may cause

771
00:59:01,365 --> 00:59:02,905
you to hear God’s message.”

772
00:59:03,645 --> 00:59:06,485
First Samuel, chapter ten.

773
00:59:06,525 --> 00:59:12,825
Then Samuel took the vial of oil and poured
it on his head, then kissed him and said,

774
00:59:13,885 --> 00:59:17,325
“Hasn’t the LORD anointed you to be prince
over his inheritance?

775
00:59:18,305 --> 00:59:24,445
When you have departed from me today, then
you will find two men by Rachel’s tomb, on

776
00:59:24,485 --> 00:59:27,245
the border of Benjamin at Zelzah.

777
00:59:27,285 --> 00:59:33,285
They will tell you, ‘The donkeys which you
went to look for have been found; and behold,

778
00:59:34,145 --> 00:59:40,365
your father has stopped caring about the
donkeys and is anxious for you, saying, “What

779
00:59:40,405 --> 00:59:46,705
shall I do for my son?”’ “Then you will
go on forward from there, and you will come to

780
00:59:46,745 --> 00:59:47,785
the oak of Tabor.

781
00:59:48,345 --> 00:59:54,505
Three men will meet you there going up
to God to Bethel: one carrying three young goats,

782
00:59:55,285 --> 01:00:00,845
and another carrying three loaves of bread,
and another carrying a container of wine.

783
01:00:01,254 --> 01:00:06,554
They will greet you and give you two
loaves of bread, which you shall receive from their

784
01:00:06,594 --> 01:00:07,494
hand.

785
01:00:07,954 --> 01:00:13,454
“After that you will come to the hill
of God, where the garrison of the Philistines is;

786
01:00:14,054 --> 01:00:19,134
and it will happen, when you have come there
to the city, that you will meet a band of

787
01:00:19,174 --> 01:00:25,354
prophets coming down from the high place with
a lute, a tambourine, a pipe, and a harp

788
01:00:25,394 --> 01:00:28,134
before them; and they will be prophesying.

789
01:00:28,654 --> 01:00:34,614
Then the LORD’s Spirit will come mightily on
you, then you will prophesy with them and

790
01:00:34,654 --> 01:00:36,354
will be turned into another man.

791
01:00:37,214 --> 01:00:42,934
Let it be, when these signs have come to
you, that you do what is appropriate for the

792
01:00:42,974 --> 01:00:45,154
occasion; for God is with you.

793
01:00:45,874 --> 01:00:52,714
“Go down ahead of me to Gilgal; and behold,
I will come down to you to offer burnt offerings

794
01:00:52,754 --> 01:00:56,254
and to sacrifice sacrifices of peace
offerings.

795
01:00:57,034 --> 01:01:02,554
Wait seven days, until I come to you and
show you what you are to do.”

796
01:01:02,994 --> 01:01:09,414
It was so, that when he had turned his
back to go from Samuel, God gave him another heart;

797
01:01:09,894 --> 01:01:12,334
and all those signs happened that day.

798
01:01:13,234 --> 01:01:19,554
When they came there to the hill, behold,
a band of prophets met him; and the Spirit

799
01:01:19,594 --> 01:01:23,614
of God came mightily on him, and he
prophesied amongst them.

800
01:01:23,654 --> 01:01:30,854
When all who knew him before saw
that, behold, he prophesied with the prophets, then

801
01:01:30,894 --> 01:01:35,794
the people said to one another, “What is
this that has come to the son of Kish?

802
01:01:36,394 --> 01:01:38,474
Is Saul also amongst the prophets?”

803
01:01:39,394 --> 01:01:42,654
One from the same place answered, “Who is
their father?”

804
01:01:43,414 --> 01:01:47,594
Therefore it became a proverb, “Is Saul
also amongst the prophets?”

805
01:01:48,354 --> 01:01:52,154
When he had finished prophesying, he came
to the high place.

806
01:01:52,974 --> 01:01:56,914
Saul’s uncle said to him and to his
servant, “Where did you go?”

807
01:01:57,594 --> 01:01:59,354
He said, “To seek the donkeys.

808
01:01:59,914 --> 01:02:03,034
When we saw that they were not found, we
came to Samuel.”

809
01:02:03,974 --> 01:02:08,014
Saul’s uncle said, “Please tell me what
Samuel said to you.”

810
01:02:08,234 --> 01:02:12,994
Saul said to his uncle, “He told us
plainly that the donkeys were found.”

811
01:02:13,834 --> 01:02:19,354
But concerning the matter of the kingdom,
of which Samuel spoke, he didn’t tell him.

812
01:02:19,615 --> 01:02:25,475
Samuel called the people together to the LORD
to Mizpah; and he said to the children

813
01:02:25,515 --> 01:02:32,955
of Israel, “The LORD, the God of Israel,
says ‘I brought Israel up out of Egypt and

814
01:02:32,995 --> 01:02:38,215
I delivered you out of the hand of the
Egyptians, and out of the hand of all the kingdoms

815
01:02:38,255 --> 01:02:39,475
that oppressed you.’

816
01:02:40,115 --> 01:02:46,155
But you have today rejected your God, who
himself saves you out of all your calamities

817
01:02:46,195 --> 01:02:50,015
and your distresses; and you have said to
him, ‘No!

818
01:02:50,055 --> 01:02:52,115
Set a king over us!’

819
01:02:52,975 --> 01:02:58,335
Now therefore present yourselves before the LORD
by your tribes and by your thousands.”

820
01:02:59,375 --> 01:03:04,635
So Samuel brought all the tribes of Israel
near, and the tribe of Benjamin was chosen.

821
01:03:05,675 --> 01:03:11,095
He brought the tribe of Benjamin near by
their families and the family of the Matrites

822
01:03:11,135 --> 01:03:12,035
was chosen.

823
01:03:12,975 --> 01:03:18,755
Then Saul the son of Kish was chosen; but
when they looked for him, he could not be found.

824
01:03:19,495 --> 01:03:24,235
Therefore they asked of the LORD further,
“Is there yet a man to come here?”

825
01:03:25,215 --> 01:03:30,235
The LORD answered, “Behold, he has hidden
himself amongst the baggage.”

826
01:03:31,175 --> 01:03:32,695
They ran and got him there.

827
01:03:32,735 --> 01:03:38,135
When he stood amongst the people, he was
higher than any of the people from his shoulders

828
01:03:38,175 --> 01:03:39,075
and upward.

829
01:03:39,495 --> 01:03:45,775
Samuel said to all the people, “Do you see
him whom the LORD has chosen, that there is

830
01:03:45,815 --> 01:03:48,195
no one like him amongst all the people?”

831
01:03:48,975 --> 01:03:52,955
All the people shouted and said, “Long
live the king!”

832
01:03:53,715 --> 01:03:59,315
Then Samuel told the people the regulations of
the kingdom, and wrote it in a book and

833
01:03:59,355 --> 01:04:00,955
laid it up before the LORD.

834
01:04:01,955 --> 01:04:06,475
Samuel sent all the people away, every man
to his house.

835
01:04:06,955 --> 01:04:13,115
Saul also went to his house in Gibeah; and
the army went with him, whose hearts God had

836
01:04:13,155 --> 01:04:13,455
touched.

837
01:04:13,495 --> 01:04:18,375
But certain worthless fellows said, “How
could this man save us?”

838
01:04:19,375 --> 01:04:22,235
They despised him, and brought him no
tribute.

839
01:04:23,175 --> 01:04:24,335
But he held his peace.

840
01:04:24,375 --> 01:04:28,415
First Samuel, chapter eleven.

841
01:04:28,455 --> 01:04:34,515
Then Nahash the Ammonite came up and
encamped against Jabesh Gilead; and all the men

842
01:04:34,555 --> 01:04:40,435
of Jabesh said to Nahash, “Make a covenant
with us, and we will serve you.”

843
01:04:40,695 --> 01:04:47,355
Nahash the Ammonite said to them, “On this
condition I will make it with you, that all

844
01:04:47,395 --> 01:04:49,355
your right eyes be gouged out.

845
01:04:50,255 --> 01:04:52,715
I will make this dishonour all Israel.”

846
01:04:53,775 --> 01:05:00,495
The elders of Jabesh said to him, “Give us
seven days, that we may send messengers to

847
01:05:00,535 --> 01:05:06,795
all the borders of Israel; and then, if there
